IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccsa-services`

-- Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA), ss 4, 5B, 9, 18, 21, 22(3), 25, 29, 36, 45, 45A, read with the Education and Care
-- Services National Law (WA) s 5 and s 103 -- worked cases from the seat of the parent using child care.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or the Child Care Services regulations (not deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_wa_child-care-services-act-2007_baseline.py). Expected results
-- were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe): c066 (10 February 2031), Oliver, under one,
-- in long day care three days a week. That the centre is run by a business and falls in none of the National Law's
-- exclusions is ASSUMED (the scenario says only "long day care"). The grandmother, the family friend, the swimming
-- school and both creches are the encoder's illustrations, not scenario events; the creches are ILLUSTRATIVE because the
-- regulations that prescribe types of service (s 4(b)) and the National Law's prescribed classes are not deposited.

`Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`an outside school hours care service` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a family member or guardian, personally`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a family friend minding him, unadvertised` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a family friend, personally, informally, with no advertised offer`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a family friend who advertised the offer` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a family friend who advertised the offer`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a swimming school` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `instruction in a particular activity`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS FALSE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `a prescribed disability service or other prescribed class`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS TRUE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

`a creche beside an approved centre, run by its approved provider (illustrative)` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `a prescribed disability service or other prescribed class`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS TRUE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS TRUE

`a centre prescribed under this Act but not excluded from the National Law` MEANS Service WITH
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis` IS TRUE
    `the children are under 13` IS TRUE
    `who gives the care` IS `a business, organisation or public body`
    `the exclusion` IS `none of the exclusions`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS TRUE
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS FALSE

§ `ss 4, 5B -- which law governs the service`

-- c066: Oliver's long day care is an education and care service under the National Law, so this Act does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)` EQUALS `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `an outside school hours care service` EQUALS `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` EQUALS `neither this Act nor the National Law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `a family friend minding him, unadvertised` EQUALS `neither this Act nor the National Law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `a family friend who advertised the offer` EQUALS `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `a swimming school` EQUALS `neither this Act nor the National Law`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` EQUALS `this Act, as a child care service`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `a creche beside an approved centre, run by its approved provider (illustrative)` EQUALS `this Act, as an associated children's service, so far as the National Law does not apply`
#ASSERT `Which law governs the service my child attends` `a centre prescribed under this Act but not excluded from the National Law` EQUALS `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`

#ASSERT NOT `Is it a child care service under this Act` `Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)`
#ASSERT `Is it a child care service under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)`

§ `ss 9, 45, 5B(2) -- must it be licensed`

-- c066: no licence under this Act; the National Law's service approval is what Oliver's centre needs.
#ASSERT `Must the service hold a licence` `Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)` FALSE EQUALS `none under this Act: the National Law requires a provider approval and service approval instead (s 103)`
#ASSERT `Must the service hold a licence` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` FALSE EQUALS `a licence under s 9 for this service at this place`
#ASSERT `Must the service hold a licence` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` TRUE EQUALS `none: it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order under s 45`
#ASSERT `Must the service hold a licence` `a creche beside an approved centre, run by its approved provider (illustrative)` FALSE EQUALS `its National Law service approval counts as its licence (s 5B(2))`
#ASSERT `Must the service hold a licence` `Oliver's grandmother minding him herself` FALSE EQUALS `none: neither this Act nor the National Law requires one`

§ `ss 13, 21, 22(3), 45(3B) -- is it lawfully provided`

#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `in effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: under a licence that has effect`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `its period has ended, but a renewal was lodged in time and is undecided` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: under a licence that has effect`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `its period has ended and no renewal was lodged in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: provided without a licence that has effect for it here (s 9 offence)`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: provided without a licence that has effect for it here (s 9 offence)`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `in effect` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: provided without a licence that has effect for it here (s 9 offence)`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `in effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: provided in breach of the licence (s 9; s 20 offence)`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: under a Ministerial exemption`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `a creche the National Law excludes and the regulations prescribe (illustrative)` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: provided in breach of the exemption's conditions (s 45(3B) offence)`
#ASSERT `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` `Oliver's long day care, three days a week (c066)` `no licence held` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not for this Act: the National Law governs it`

§ `s 9 penalty`

#ASSERT `What is the most the provider can be fined for running unlicensed` TRUE EQUALS 12000
#ASSERT `What is the most the provider can be fined for running unlicensed` FALSE EQUALS 24000

#ASSERT `What is the daily penalty for running unlicensed` FALSE EQUALS 1200

